course: dictionary
lesson: 5048
title: Innocent: not guilty, not knowing, not meant to harm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Innocent has several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. In a court or a story, innocent means not guilty: the person did not do the wrong thing they are blamed for. In law, people are innocent until a court decides they did it.
explain: Innocent can also mean young and trusting, not yet knowing about bad or unkind things. It can mean not meant to harm, as in «an innocent joke», where nobody wanted to hurt anyone. To check your meaning, swap in a simple word such as not guilty, trusting or harmless, and see if the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Innocent appears in useful phrases. «Innocent of» something means you did not do it. «Innocent until proven guilty» is a rule that protects people. As a noun, an innocent is a person who has done nothing wrong, especially someone hurt in a war or a crime.
fact: Innocent means not guilty, not knowing about bad things, or not meant to harm.
fact: «Innocent until proven guilty» means a person is treated as not guilty until a court decides otherwise.
fact: «Charged» means a person has been accused of a crime; a court decides if he did it.
fact: «An innocent mistake» was made by accident, not on purpose.
fact: Being «framed» means being blamed for something you did not do, and «setting the record straight» means telling the truth afterwards.
exercise: «The judge said the man was innocent, so he went home free.» What does innocent mean here? | Very angry | Very funny | *Not guilty | Very young
exercise: «It was an innocent mistake; she never meant to break the vase.» What does innocent suggest? | *Not done on purpose | Done with great anger | Repeated many times | Hidden in a box
exercise: Find and copy the one word that means not meant to harm: «It was only an innocent joke.» | was | only | joke | *innocent
test: Sam is innocent of stealing the bike. What does innocent mean? | Very tired from the walk | Quick at running | *Not guilty of stealing | Unhappy about the weather
test: What does «innocent until proven guilty» mean? | A person is guilty as soon as they are accused | Nobody can ever be proven guilty | *A person is treated as not guilty until a court decides | Only children can be innocent
exam: In «an innocent joke», what does innocent mean? | Very slow | Not guilty of a crime | Very clever | *Not meant to harm
